  {"kind": "narration", "speaker_id": null, "text": "At Old Bram’s farm, the midnight hush is broken by the rustle of straw as Ash shifts closer, lantern-light catching the furrow in their brow — then Ash turns to Wren, voice low, and begins to speak of the tales of Ember Vale.", "cited_fact_keys": ["spots", "attempt:communicate", "reaction:1"]},
  {"kind": "narration", "speaker_id": null, "text": "Wren stands, arms crossed, listening — then replies, matching Ash’s quiet tone with their own telling of the same Ember Vale tales, their words weaving between them like smoke.", "cited_fact_keys": ["reaction:2", "attempt:communicate"]}
